# Trim the docker build context for the smoke-test image. Keeps the
# build under ~10 s of `COPY .` instead of ~minute for a fresh clone
# of the full tree.
#
# What's NOT excluded (kept on purpose):
#   - codegen/                — needed by scripts/regen.sh
#   - scripts/                — regen.sh runs in-image
#   - src/                    — runtime helpers the codegen emits into
#   - gleam.toml / manifest.toml — at repo root for the SDK package
#   - vendor/aws-sdk-rust/aws-models/ — Smithy models the codegen
#                                       reads from
#   - vendor/smithy/          — protocol-test fixtures (small)
#   - smoke-test/             — the smoke test itself

# Heavy local-only state
.git
build
*/build
smoke-test/build
codegen/build

# Generated SDK services. These are gitignored and are regenerated
# inside the image by `./scripts/regen.sh s3 sqs` (Dockerfile RUN
# step). If the host's prior full-regen output COPYed in, Gleam
# would compile all 409 services and OOM the docker build.
src/aws/services
src/aws/services/protocoltests
test/protocol_tests
test/fixtures

erl_crash.dump
*/erl_crash.dump
.tools
.claude

# Vendored aws-sdk-rust subtree we don't need at codegen time:
# the SDK source itself (~600 MB). Only the aws-models/ JSON files
# under it are read by ./scripts/regen.sh.
vendor/aws-sdk-rust/sdk
vendor/aws-sdk-rust/tools
vendor/aws-sdk-rust/tests
vendor/aws-sdk-rust/examples
vendor/aws-sdk-rust/.git*
